WEBVTT

00:13.680 --> 00:15.265
‎I'm Akine Atagawa.

00:16.474 --> 00:17.517
‎I look forward to...

00:18.893 --> 00:20.687
‎getting to know you.

00:21.938 --> 00:22.939
‎Younger sister...

00:24.065 --> 00:25.692
‎She's Manatsu Atagawa's younger sister?

01:57.534 --> 02:01.955
‎EPISODE 11
‎INVERSION

02:02.664 --> 02:04.249
‎I'm Manatsu Atagawa.

02:04.332 --> 02:05.667
‎I used to play youth basketball.

02:06.167 --> 02:07.669
‎Nice to meet you.

02:08.545 --> 02:09.879
‎Nice to meet you.

02:11.297 --> 02:12.924
‎Back in my first year of middle school,

02:13.007 --> 02:17.762
‎I joined the basketball team
‎after my neighbor, Sacchan, invited me.

02:17.846 --> 02:19.180
‎Koyuki!

02:19.264 --> 02:20.932
‎Thanks for coming.

02:21.432 --> 02:23.059
‎Sorry I'm not Miki.

02:23.143 --> 02:26.646
‎-I'm just happy to have you.
‎-Attack!

02:26.729 --> 02:28.106
‎MIKI JOINED THE VOLLEYBALL TEAM

02:28.189 --> 02:29.190
‎Is she a friend, Sachi?

02:29.274 --> 02:30.650
‎Glad to have you on the team.

02:30.733 --> 02:31.943
‎I'll do my best.

02:32.026 --> 02:34.070
‎-Let's do this!
‎-We'll make a great team!

02:34.154 --> 02:36.197
‎My seniors were kind.

02:36.281 --> 02:37.198
‎GRADE 3 CLASS 1

02:37.282 --> 02:38.366
‎Here.

02:38.449 --> 02:40.785
‎The second and third years
‎will be on the court today.

02:40.869 --> 02:43.121
‎This is a set menu
‎for the first years to practice.

02:43.204 --> 02:44.205
‎Okay.

02:44.914 --> 02:47.667
‎I was glad to have someone I knew.

02:47.750 --> 02:49.169
‎Thanks!

02:51.921 --> 02:53.214
‎Koyuki.

02:53.298 --> 02:54.924
‎Come back soon, 'kay?

02:56.050 --> 02:57.051
‎BOW

02:57.135 --> 02:58.136
‎Such a cutie.

02:58.219 --> 02:59.220
‎Stop bothering her!

02:59.304 --> 03:01.347
‎Which is why I didn't notice it sooner.

03:01.431 --> 03:03.224
‎-Don't do that.
‎-Why not?

03:03.308 --> 03:05.018
‎She didn't like it.

03:05.101 --> 03:06.311
‎What was that?

03:06.811 --> 03:08.229
‎GIRLS BASKETBALL CLUB

03:08.313 --> 03:10.440
‎Only the first years
‎are practicing outside today.

03:10.523 --> 03:13.192
‎The captain gave me a set menu
‎that we can practice from.

03:13.276 --> 03:14.277
‎Hey.

03:15.528 --> 03:17.447
‎Who died and put you in charge?

03:19.532 --> 03:23.536
‎At first, I thought she just
‎didn't like being told what to do.

03:24.829 --> 03:25.955
‎But then...

03:26.039 --> 03:27.749
‎How are we gonna get you taller?

03:27.832 --> 03:28.833
‎CHATTER - STRETCH

03:28.917 --> 03:30.877
‎-Isn't that stretching her neck?
‎-What to do.

03:30.960 --> 03:33.588
‎Then I realized her hostility toward me

03:33.671 --> 03:35.715
‎was because of my affinity
‎with the seniors.

03:38.301 --> 03:42.722
‎Manatsu must think it's weird
‎that I'm so close with Sacchan.

03:42.805 --> 03:44.140
‎CHILDHOOD FRIENDS - CLOSE FRIENDS

03:44.224 --> 03:46.226
‎HOSTILE
‎"I'M BETTER THAN HER"

03:48.228 --> 03:49.229
‎Manatsu.

03:49.896 --> 03:53.816
‎The captain wants to see me during lunch.
‎Would you mind coming with me?

03:56.945 --> 03:58.196
‎Thanks for coming.

03:58.279 --> 04:01.532
‎I don't always feel comfortable going
‎to the third-year classroom on my own.

04:03.534 --> 04:06.454
‎Why does the captain
‎always want to talk to you?

04:06.537 --> 04:08.414
‎I'm just easy to talk to for her, is all.

04:08.498 --> 04:12.210
‎We live nearby, and we've never had any
‎of those regular formalities to limit us.

04:12.919 --> 04:16.339
‎I think you're the one she's got
‎her hopes set on for the team, Manatsu.

04:17.548 --> 04:18.549
‎You think?

04:19.175 --> 04:20.593
‎GRADE 3 CLASS 1

04:21.177 --> 04:23.304
‎Manatsu today as well? Thanks for coming.

04:24.847 --> 04:26.224
‎Are you Koyuki's friend?

04:26.307 --> 04:27.517
‎Don't talk to them. Go away.

04:28.726 --> 04:30.061
‎Yes. My name is Manatsu.

04:30.770 --> 04:32.021
‎So we're friends now?

04:33.106 --> 04:34.274
‎You know what?

04:34.357 --> 04:36.567
‎You're a really great friend.

04:36.651 --> 04:38.278
‎I had you all wrong.

04:38.361 --> 04:39.362
‎Oh, yeah?

04:39.445 --> 04:40.446
‎THANKS, BUT...

04:40.530 --> 04:41.781
‎How did you get to that conclusion?

04:41.864 --> 04:44.409
‎So just "Manatsu" from now on.
‎No more honorifics.

04:45.535 --> 04:49.122
‎Being on Manatsu's good side
‎definitely made club activities easier.

04:49.205 --> 04:50.206
‎Keep your chin up!

04:50.290 --> 04:51.291
‎UM...

04:51.374 --> 04:54.877
‎Manatsu got her chance to talk with the
‎seniors whenever she was with me.

04:54.961 --> 04:57.005
‎-What did you have for lunch?
‎-Hello!

04:57.088 --> 05:00.967
‎We weren't friends based on mutual trust.
‎I was just convenient.

05:02.135 --> 05:05.722
‎So there wasn't any one particular event
‎that caused our friendship to break down.

05:05.805 --> 05:06.806
‎GIRLS BASKETBALL CLUB

05:07.390 --> 05:10.393
‎So of the people in our grade,
‎Hotani and Igarashi are pretty hot, hey?

05:10.476 --> 05:11.561
‎Definitely.

05:11.644 --> 05:12.645
‎KOYUKI'S IMAGE

05:12.729 --> 05:13.813
‎IGARASHI
‎BOTHERS ME FOR NO REASON

05:13.896 --> 05:15.064
‎HOTANI
‎IGARASHI'S RIGHT-HAND MAN

05:15.148 --> 05:16.941
‎And what's your type, Koyuki?

05:17.025 --> 05:19.402
‎I can't even imagine what yours could be.

05:21.195 --> 05:23.406
‎Maybe someone
‎who doesn't make fun of others?

05:23.489 --> 05:26.659
‎We're talking about looks here.
‎Weren't you listening?

05:27.702 --> 05:28.703
‎Oh, right.

05:30.705 --> 05:32.040
‎I have no idea.

05:32.123 --> 05:33.416
‎Okay...

05:33.499 --> 05:36.377
‎AWKWARD SILENCE

05:36.878 --> 05:38.046
‎I'll see you later.

05:38.129 --> 05:39.422
‎-See you.
‎-Bye.

05:43.301 --> 05:45.178
‎That Koyuki girl...

05:45.928 --> 05:47.930
‎She's kind of different, isn't she?

05:48.014 --> 05:50.975
‎Yeah, I feel you.
‎She's kind of gloomy, right?

05:51.059 --> 05:52.060
‎That's it!

05:52.143 --> 05:55.813
‎And I got really annoyed at how slow
‎she was to talk just now. Did you notice?

05:55.897 --> 05:58.316
‎-Like, gimme an answer, girl!
‎-Yes!

05:58.399 --> 06:01.694
‎Our friendship
‎had always been a house of cards.

06:02.278 --> 06:04.363
‎You're a really great friend.

06:05.281 --> 06:07.700
‎She didn't mean for my personality.

06:08.576 --> 06:10.995
‎She meant that I was convenient.

06:12.830 --> 06:14.207
‎You sure do love your grunt work.

06:14.791 --> 06:17.335
‎Surely you have other things to do?

06:18.920 --> 06:20.463
‎She's eating on her own.

06:20.546 --> 06:23.716
‎Her water bottle is so lame.
‎Like, it literally makes me laugh.

06:24.717 --> 06:28.721
‎So it didn't take long
‎for me to be branded as the bad guy.

06:31.307 --> 06:33.935
‎I can't take this anymore.
‎I'm going to quit.

06:35.061 --> 06:38.648
‎I should have just quit
‎and cut all ties with her right away.

06:38.731 --> 06:39.732
‎CLUB WITHDRAWAL FORM

06:40.608 --> 06:41.734
‎You know what?

06:42.401 --> 06:45.488
‎Atagawa's been really
‎coming on strong with me lately.

06:47.073 --> 06:50.576
‎I'm not interested in anyone
‎other than the person I like.

06:51.077 --> 06:52.245
‎It's getting annoying.

06:54.330 --> 06:56.833
‎Manatsu likes Igarashi?

06:59.127 --> 07:00.628
‎Do you understand what I'm saying?

07:04.340 --> 07:06.300
‎Please go out with me, Koyuki.

07:07.343 --> 07:10.263
‎Honestly,
‎the first thing that came to mind was,

07:10.930 --> 07:12.765
‎"He finally said it."

07:13.474 --> 07:16.018
‎And, "Please let go of my hand."

07:16.102 --> 07:17.103
‎STARE

07:17.186 --> 07:20.273
‎And, "He's acting like rejection
‎isn't even in the cards for him."

07:20.982 --> 07:25.528
‎-And, "Why does he even like me?"
‎-Koyuki.

07:25.611 --> 07:27.155
‎-‎All these thoughts...
‎-Koyuki.

07:28.990 --> 07:32.994
‎I felt I needed something more
‎than simply cutting ties.

07:34.203 --> 07:35.204
‎Which is why...

07:35.288 --> 07:36.289
‎Okay.

07:36.789 --> 07:40.585
‎I felt my body, my heart,
‎screaming at me to stop...

07:41.544 --> 07:43.045
‎I'll go out with you.

07:43.129 --> 07:46.340
‎I just pretended I didn't hear it.

07:47.508 --> 07:48.676
‎Not again.

07:49.510 --> 07:52.221
‎I quit the club
‎and started dating Igarashi,

07:52.305 --> 07:55.433
‎and from then on,
‎nothing ever happened directly,

07:55.516 --> 07:57.768
‎but the indirect harassment increased.

07:58.478 --> 08:02.231
‎Probably because she didn't want Igarashi
‎or the boys to know what she was doing.

08:03.274 --> 08:06.777
‎I needed something to prove
‎Manatsu was the one behind it all.

08:06.861 --> 08:08.196
‎Morning, Koyun.

08:08.779 --> 08:11.782
‎For once, I got here with time to spare...

08:12.283 --> 08:13.284
‎What...

08:16.537 --> 08:18.956
‎Atagawa...

08:19.040 --> 08:20.249
‎Let go of me!

08:27.465 --> 08:28.466
‎The glass!

08:28.549 --> 08:31.010
‎Miki, you're bleeding!
‎We gotta get you cleaned up.

08:31.093 --> 08:32.553
‎No, wait!

08:32.637 --> 08:34.013
‎What? Blood?

08:34.096 --> 08:35.097
‎Was there a fight?

08:40.186 --> 08:41.521
‎Well, look at you.

08:41.604 --> 08:44.482
‎Hiding first behind the boys,
‎and now Miki?

08:44.565 --> 08:48.986
‎You go around with this "poor me" act
‎and you literally leech off others.

08:49.070 --> 08:50.363
‎Aren't you ashamed?

08:51.822 --> 08:52.865
‎Not really.

08:53.491 --> 08:56.285
‎At least I don't go around
‎harassing people in childish ways.

08:56.369 --> 08:57.954
‎I'd be more ashamed of that.

08:59.038 --> 09:01.249
‎I told you. That wasn't me.

09:01.332 --> 09:03.251
‎Who else would do it but you?

09:03.334 --> 09:05.002
‎How should I know?

09:05.086 --> 09:07.129
‎Plenty of people
‎pass by those shoe lockers.

09:07.213 --> 09:08.297
‎Are you really that stupid?

09:10.675 --> 09:12.385
‎-I never mentioned that.
‎-What?

09:12.468 --> 09:16.639
‎Nobody ever said anything
‎about this being in my shoe locker.

09:17.723 --> 09:19.141
‎Hey, over here!

09:19.725 --> 09:21.352
‎Here! Over here!

09:22.770 --> 09:24.647
‎You dug your own grave, Manatsu.

09:24.730 --> 09:25.898
‎Come on.

09:25.982 --> 09:27.400
‎Are you really that stupid?

09:27.483 --> 09:28.526
‎Come on!

09:29.610 --> 09:30.945
‎Listen, you!

09:31.028 --> 09:34.615
‎You've got some nerve ditching the club
‎to start your own little clique.

09:34.699 --> 09:37.868
‎We all know deep down you're just a gloomy
‎loner who can't do anything on her own.

09:38.578 --> 09:39.620
‎Stay like that.

09:39.704 --> 09:40.871
‎What are you smiling at?

09:40.955 --> 09:42.206
‎What are you doing?

09:43.499 --> 09:44.500
‎Igarashi?

09:44.584 --> 09:47.628
‎Hey, hey, hey...

09:48.671 --> 09:51.382
‎The hell is this?
‎What are you doing to her, Atagawa?

09:52.258 --> 09:53.593
‎Are you all right, Koyuki?

09:56.095 --> 09:57.388
‎That hurt.

10:02.226 --> 10:03.894
‎Way to go, Igarashi!

10:05.146 --> 10:06.314
‎You da prince!

10:07.231 --> 10:09.442
‎How lovely for you, Koyuki.

10:09.525 --> 10:12.570
‎Such sweet crocodile tears.
‎You're such a girlie girl.

10:12.653 --> 10:13.654
‎So very "cute."

10:14.822 --> 10:17.408
‎You play the victim
‎for your knight in shining armor.

10:17.491 --> 10:19.160
‎You're such a poser.

10:20.453 --> 10:23.456
‎Hey! What did you just hiss at her?

10:24.415 --> 10:25.791
‎Let's go, Koyuki.

10:28.961 --> 10:30.379
‎Manatsu Atagawa.

10:31.881 --> 10:33.799
‎Akine is her younger sister.

10:34.675 --> 10:37.803
‎Just how much does she know about me?

10:39.889 --> 10:40.890
‎FLUFFY FLUFFY

10:40.973 --> 10:42.224
‎I really hate this!

10:42.308 --> 10:45.811
‎The more I think about it,
‎the more I hate middle school.

10:45.895 --> 10:49.982
‎No, more than that...
‎I hate who I was back then.

10:54.904 --> 10:57.573
‎You're on social media now?

10:57.657 --> 11:00.326
‎Yeah, I just started
‎thanks to Miharu and Sora.

11:00.409 --> 11:02.745
‎MIHARU - SORA
‎FRIENDS FROM MIDDLE SCHOOL

11:02.828 --> 11:03.913
‎Found one.

11:03.996 --> 11:06.082
‎So this is Manatsu's sister?

11:06.165 --> 11:07.500
‎#SISTERS #BESTIES

11:07.583 --> 11:08.584
‎Besties?

11:10.211 --> 11:13.255
‎What's this?
‎Koyun and Miki. What are you up to?

11:14.674 --> 11:16.342
‎What? Atagawa?

11:17.009 --> 11:19.345
‎We're in the same class.
‎We chat all the time.

11:19.929 --> 11:23.682
‎Akine says you've told her
‎some things about me.

11:24.475 --> 11:26.602
‎What exactly have you told her?

11:26.685 --> 11:29.855
‎Just that we've been friends
‎for, like, forever?

11:30.481 --> 11:33.984
‎Koyun! If you and I get married,
‎you and Miki will be related. Cool, right?

11:34.068 --> 11:35.236
‎That's brilliant!

11:35.319 --> 11:36.695
‎Sure. Whatever.

11:36.779 --> 11:39.949
‎I said we might even
‎get married in the future.

11:40.449 --> 11:41.784
‎Why would you say that?

11:42.284 --> 11:44.703
‎Well, in the end...

11:44.787 --> 11:45.788
‎BAHA!

11:45.871 --> 11:48.624
‎...I have zero clue
‎as to what's going on in her mind.

11:48.707 --> 11:50.459
‎Atagawa's the "cool girl" type, after all.

11:51.127 --> 11:52.128
‎BWAHAHA

11:52.211 --> 11:54.463
‎She's not a bad person. Probably? Maybe?

11:55.297 --> 11:57.466
‎Or so Yuki says...

11:57.550 --> 12:01.220
‎I have no idea
‎how much she knows about me.

12:01.804 --> 12:05.474
‎She could know parts of me
‎that I don't want anyone to know.

12:05.558 --> 12:06.809
‎VARIOUS MEMORIES

12:06.892 --> 12:09.228
‎That alone makes me feel very uneasy.

12:10.062 --> 12:14.233
‎Please... Please don't let us
‎have to interact much going forward...

12:32.501 --> 12:34.044
‎Of course.

12:34.128 --> 12:36.922
‎We live in the same neighborhood.
‎Of course our school routes overlap.

12:38.132 --> 12:42.928
‎Are the first years not doing
‎morning practice for soccer yet?

12:43.512 --> 12:45.347
‎There's no morning practice today.

12:46.724 --> 12:47.766
‎Okay...

12:48.767 --> 12:50.311
‎DEAD SILENT

12:50.394 --> 12:51.687
‎This is awkward.

12:52.271 --> 12:55.983
‎At times like these, it's the older person
‎who should initiate conversation, right?

12:56.609 --> 12:58.486
‎But what do we even talk about?

12:59.862 --> 13:02.740
‎What do we have in common?
‎I don't want to talk about middle school.

13:02.823 --> 13:04.825
‎COMMONALITIES
‎TALK ABOUT MIDDLE SCHOOL

13:04.909 --> 13:05.910
‎HIGH SCHOOL LIFE

13:05.993 --> 13:08.204
‎High school life?
‎Would that even be stimulating?

13:09.580 --> 13:11.624
‎What do I do?
‎I'm so bad at making conversation.

13:11.707 --> 13:12.708
‎TOO LATE

13:16.295 --> 13:17.421
‎Morning.

13:18.756 --> 13:19.757
‎PHEW

13:19.840 --> 13:20.841
‎Amamiya.

13:21.842 --> 13:22.843
‎WHOA

13:22.927 --> 13:23.928
‎THUMP THUMP THUMP

13:24.011 --> 13:25.846
‎Why did she react like that?

13:25.930 --> 13:27.223
‎What a relief.

13:27.306 --> 13:28.682
‎Now I'm saved.

13:28.766 --> 13:30.851
‎Good morning, Amamiya.

13:31.435 --> 13:32.937
‎Are you two walking together?

13:33.437 --> 13:34.688
‎We just met on the train.

13:35.189 --> 13:38.108
‎MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

13:38.192 --> 13:40.236
‎So you like that song too?

13:40.319 --> 13:41.820
‎I listen to it all the time.

13:42.404 --> 13:45.866
‎Wow. He's doing a great job
‎keeping our conversation flowing.

13:46.617 --> 13:51.330
‎I'm sorry, Amamiya, for thinking
‎your questions were tiring back then.

13:51.997 --> 13:54.917
‎And I'm also sorry for laughing at you
‎when you were flustered.

13:55.459 --> 13:56.835
‎STARE

13:57.336 --> 13:59.213
‎What? Is there something on me?

13:59.713 --> 14:00.714
‎PFT PFT

14:00.798 --> 14:05.803
‎No, I was just thinking I feel bad for
‎teasing you that time over spring break.

14:05.886 --> 14:07.388
‎You only feel that now?

14:07.471 --> 14:11.183
‎Hey, do you think you'd forget about that
‎if I push the pressure point on your head?

14:11.267 --> 14:12.851
‎There's a pressure point that does that?

14:12.935 --> 14:14.228
‎-It's around here.
‎-I block.

14:14.311 --> 14:15.312
‎CHATTER CHATTER

14:15.396 --> 14:17.273
‎Let me find a work-around. Here...

14:17.773 --> 14:19.149
‎You're good friends, hey?

14:19.233 --> 14:23.696
‎Not at all. She's a bully.
‎She's got dirt on me.

14:23.779 --> 14:25.155
‎Hey, no...

14:31.245 --> 14:32.955
‎Good morning, Akine.

14:33.455 --> 14:34.498
‎Momoka.

14:34.582 --> 14:37.167
‎I saw you, so I came running.

14:37.251 --> 14:39.670
‎Wow, she looks just like a doll.

14:40.254 --> 14:42.923
‎And Amamiya. Good morning to you too.

14:43.799 --> 14:47.428
‎Kuriki, right? I remember you
‎from when you came to check out our club.

14:47.511 --> 14:49.805
‎You remember me?

14:50.347 --> 14:55.185
‎I decided not to join after all,
‎so I haven't been back.

14:55.769 --> 14:57.646
‎That's fine. Don't worry about that.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.440
‎Atagawa's joined, after all.

14:59.523 --> 15:01.233
‎But I...

15:01.317 --> 15:03.569
‎I think you'll do great, Akine.

15:04.069 --> 15:05.362
‎She's luminous.

15:06.280 --> 15:07.448
‎SNAP

15:09.909 --> 15:11.702
‎I know this feeling.

15:11.785 --> 15:14.580
‎I don't think I'm welcome here.

15:15.289 --> 15:17.541
‎I'll just leave for class then.

15:21.420 --> 15:22.588
‎What?

15:25.674 --> 15:28.093
‎Well then, Amamiya. See you later.

15:28.677 --> 15:30.095
‎See you at cheer training.

15:34.767 --> 15:35.768
‎Why'd you do that?

15:35.851 --> 15:40.022
‎I figured you were going
‎to just float off again.

15:41.857 --> 15:42.858
‎HEH

15:42.942 --> 15:44.902
‎-You got me.
‎-You're very obvious.

15:47.237 --> 15:48.238
‎WHOOSH WHOOSH

15:48.322 --> 15:51.200
‎You know, I kind of feel like a dog
‎being taken for walkies.

15:51.283 --> 15:52.534
‎Shall we go for run by the river?

15:52.618 --> 15:54.244
‎PONTA

15:54.328 --> 15:55.412
‎No running.

15:56.956 --> 16:00.918
‎I didn't think Amamiya would remember me.

16:01.502 --> 16:04.505
‎Because you only went once, right?

16:04.588 --> 16:06.507
‎I went twice.

16:07.257 --> 16:08.258
‎All right.

16:09.134 --> 16:10.761
‎Hey, Akine.

16:11.261 --> 16:14.682
‎Do you think Amamiya has a girlfriend?

16:16.141 --> 16:18.143
‎CHATTER CHATTER

16:18.727 --> 16:20.145
‎Who knows?

16:21.021 --> 16:22.398
‎Could you find out for me?

16:26.652 --> 16:29.154
‎Enjoying your new class?

16:31.740 --> 16:35.285
‎I don't like the way
‎you keep grinning at me.

16:35.369 --> 16:37.162
‎IRREGULAR CATCH UP OVER A MEAL

16:37.746 --> 16:40.791
‎When you're happy, Yota, I'm happy.

16:41.291 --> 16:43.669
‎Now you look like a Buddha statue.

16:45.462 --> 16:48.173
‎I didn't realize I was such a sticky beak.

16:48.966 --> 16:51.010
‎I could ask the same. How about you?

16:51.093 --> 16:53.303
‎What? No. Never.

16:53.387 --> 16:54.388
‎HMPH

16:54.471 --> 16:56.181
‎Now you're a wrathful deity...

16:56.265 --> 16:59.101
‎There was one guy in middle school.

16:59.184 --> 17:01.186
‎We dated for a little bit.

17:02.187 --> 17:04.940
‎I tried to get to know him,
‎even if only a little.

17:05.607 --> 17:09.319
‎I went out with him
‎assuming the love would eventually follow.

17:09.903 --> 17:11.572
‎But it didn't go well at all.

17:12.406 --> 17:17.828
‎I realized love
‎isn't something you can force.

17:17.911 --> 17:19.329
‎IMPURE MOTIVES

17:19.413 --> 17:21.832
‎And that wasn't the only reason
‎we started dating...

17:21.915 --> 17:22.916
‎BUT SURELY YOU?

17:23.000 --> 17:25.586
‎-But that's not the case with you, right?
‎-Don't ask me.

17:25.669 --> 17:26.670
‎LOVE

17:26.754 --> 17:29.089
‎Love can come in all shapes and sizes.

17:29.173 --> 17:32.634
‎If two kinds of love don't match,
‎one person is bound to suffer.

17:32.718 --> 17:34.470
‎WHAT? - I LOVE YOU
‎DIFFERENT TYPE

17:34.553 --> 17:36.055
‎LIKE - LOVE
‎DIFFERENT SIZE

17:36.138 --> 17:39.933
‎It's hard, because it's not enough
‎to just be liked, or to just love.

17:40.017 --> 17:41.226
‎I'M THE ONLY ONE IN PAIN

17:41.310 --> 17:43.854
‎I guess love
‎is still a long ways off for me.

17:43.937 --> 17:44.938
‎CREEP CREEP

17:45.022 --> 17:46.231
‎Soot, soot...

17:46.315 --> 17:48.817
‎LIVING IT NOW

17:48.901 --> 17:50.736
‎-That hurts to hear.
‎-‎Soot, soot...

17:51.612 --> 17:53.739
‎-Go away! Get lost!
‎-‎Soot, soot...

17:55.741 --> 17:56.742
‎I'm sorry.

17:56.825 --> 17:57.826
‎GYOZA FESTIVAL
‎EVEN MORE GYOZA

17:57.910 --> 18:00.162
‎-I didn't mean it that way.
‎-I said it's fine.

18:00.245 --> 18:01.663
‎Those were some tasty gyoza.

18:01.747 --> 18:02.748
‎How about gyoza?

18:02.831 --> 18:05.209
‎But then our breath will smell.

18:05.292 --> 18:07.294
‎They're from our school.

18:08.462 --> 18:10.380
‎RUSH RUSH

18:12.466 --> 18:14.885
‎Seniors. How awkward.

18:15.385 --> 18:17.763
‎And on a gyoza date.
‎Kinda low-key cool, hey?

18:17.846 --> 18:19.389
‎That girl just now...

18:23.310 --> 18:25.270
‎Sorry if my breath stinks.

18:25.354 --> 18:27.815
‎Mine stinks too, so I couldn't tell.

18:41.120 --> 18:42.371
‎Good morning.

18:42.955 --> 18:44.665
‎You scared me!

18:44.748 --> 18:47.251
‎You shouldn't walk and read.
‎It's dangerous.

18:47.960 --> 18:48.961
‎CLOSE

18:49.044 --> 18:50.504
‎-Tsk.
‎-Don't "tsk" me.

18:51.088 --> 18:52.381
‎What were you reading?

18:52.464 --> 18:53.799
‎I...

18:53.882 --> 18:55.259
‎THE CURIOUS CASE
‎OF THE PET MANOR

18:55.342 --> 18:56.552
‎What's this? Looks lame.

18:56.635 --> 18:58.387
‎NERVOUS WHEN TALKING ABOUT
‎THE THINGS SHE LIKES WITH OTHERS

18:58.470 --> 18:59.596
‎Hey, I know that one.

19:00.722 --> 19:02.891
‎I haven't read the book,
‎but I've seen the movie.

19:03.392 --> 19:04.393
‎It's a good story, hey?

19:05.018 --> 19:06.395
‎MELTS

19:07.062 --> 19:09.982
‎There's another movie based on a book
‎by the same author airing on TV this week.

19:10.065 --> 19:12.401
‎Yes. I saw that one in theaters.

19:12.985 --> 19:14.987
‎I liked the original,

19:15.070 --> 19:18.157
‎so I was excited to see
‎how they'd adapt it for the screen.

19:18.240 --> 19:20.659
‎Hey, she's in a good mood.

19:21.160 --> 19:23.412
‎Well, if you recommend it,
‎I'll have to give it a watch.

19:25.414 --> 19:26.915
‎She seems happy?

19:29.585 --> 19:31.086
‎She's cute.

19:32.337 --> 19:34.464
‎But sorry in advance
‎if it's not to your liking.

19:34.548 --> 19:36.550
‎EMOTIONS GRAPH
‎I MAY HAVE SET THE BAR TOO HIGH

19:36.633 --> 19:38.510
‎Why so negative? It'll be fine.

19:45.267 --> 19:48.145
‎Amamiya! Good morning.

19:48.228 --> 19:50.480
‎Kuriki. Good morning.

19:50.564 --> 19:53.609
‎Are you going
‎to this morning's cheer practice?

19:53.692 --> 19:55.736
‎No, I have club activities.

19:56.236 --> 19:58.155
‎But you're in the cheer squad.
‎Right, Koyun?

19:58.238 --> 19:59.656
‎Yeah.

20:00.532 --> 20:02.117
‎Koyun?

20:04.369 --> 20:05.370
‎Good morning.

20:06.371 --> 20:07.915
‎THE CONVERSATION DIED

20:10.542 --> 20:11.585
‎Koyun.

20:12.085 --> 20:13.629
‎It sounds so strange.

20:13.712 --> 20:16.924
‎I saw you yesterday, right?
‎Outside the restaurant.

20:17.007 --> 20:18.508
‎Yeah, you did.

20:19.009 --> 20:21.178
‎I didn't think she'd recognize me.

20:21.261 --> 20:25.182
‎That tall guy you were with,
‎was he your boyfriend?

20:26.266 --> 20:28.310
‎No, we're just friends.

20:28.393 --> 20:32.439
‎But you looked so good together.
‎I thought you were a couple.

20:33.357 --> 20:35.525
‎I don't remember much about him though.

20:36.652 --> 20:39.446
‎No way... Is that how people see us?

20:40.030 --> 20:41.740
‎This is a troublesome misunderstanding.

20:41.823 --> 20:43.200
‎Yay!

20:43.283 --> 20:46.620
‎I mean it.
‎It really isn't like that between us.

20:46.703 --> 20:48.455
‎We're really just good friends.

20:48.538 --> 20:51.458
‎That sounds so nice.

20:51.541 --> 20:57.005
‎Then do you and Amamiya ever go out
‎for meals like that? Just the two of you?

20:59.549 --> 21:00.968
‎Just the two of us?

21:01.051 --> 21:02.970
‎-Not really.
‎-No.

21:03.053 --> 21:04.304
‎We could?

21:04.388 --> 21:05.847
‎It's okay. Don't force it.

21:06.932 --> 21:08.475
‎But I'm being serious.

21:12.145 --> 21:15.565
‎I don't want to pry
‎into other people's private lives.

21:15.649 --> 21:16.942
‎You can ask him yourself.

21:17.025 --> 21:19.194
‎You're mean.

21:21.113 --> 21:23.156
‎Is your girlfriend
‎strict about that sort of thing?

21:23.240 --> 21:25.450
‎What? No, I don't even have a girlfriend.

21:25.534 --> 21:26.660
‎Wow, really?

21:26.743 --> 21:29.329
‎But you seem like you'd be
‎super popular with the ladies.

21:29.413 --> 21:31.123
‎Don't you agree, Koyun?

21:31.707 --> 21:32.708
‎-WE BROKE UP.
‎-AGAIN?

21:32.791 --> 21:33.875
‎CONVERSATION FROM A WHILE BACK

21:33.959 --> 21:34.960
‎Yeah, I think so.

21:35.544 --> 21:37.462
‎You do seem to have
‎a lot of dating experience.

21:39.047 --> 21:41.258
‎I do not! Not at all!

21:42.259 --> 21:44.803
‎Methinks the man doth protest too much...

21:46.471 --> 21:47.514
‎You're right.

21:47.597 --> 21:48.724
‎Hey.

21:48.807 --> 21:50.976
‎Hey, wait...

21:51.476 --> 21:53.437
‎Is that really the impression I give?

21:59.234 --> 22:01.862
‎And what would make him protest so much...

23:33.995 --> 23:36.164
‎GRADE 1 CLASS 1

23:39.668 --> 23:40.919
‎Akine.

23:41.002 --> 23:42.003
‎LA-DI-DA

23:42.087 --> 23:43.755
‎Amamiya says he doesn't have a girlfriend.

23:43.839 --> 23:45.674
‎And you came to tell me because?

23:47.676 --> 23:50.512
‎So isn't this your big chance?

23:52.305 --> 23:53.431
‎You're right!

23:53.932 --> 23:55.934
‎Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
